{"step_index":306,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-02T14:02:12Z","thinking":"The initial server response confirms `index.html` is served, indicating the basic setup is functional. The plan shifts toward comprehensive end-to-end testing with a script that simulates user interactions. Authentication is the primary focus, aiming to verify both registration and login, including both valid and invalid credential scenarios, with a focus on observing the proper response status codes.\n\n\nFirst, the system will obtain an authenticated user profile to establish a baseline. Following this, the user profile will be updated to reflect the desired currency preference. Then, the budget management system will be verified by setting a monthly budget and assessing the initial metrics.\n\nNext, bills across multiple categories will be created, and the system's ability to automatically assign statuses (Overdue/Pending) will be verified. After that, a 'Mark as Paid' function will be tested, and a monthly bill summary will be tested to ensure the bill summary accurately reflects the data entered.\n\nFinally, expense management is addressed: Various expenses will be added, search functionality tested, total expenses calculated, and finally, testing the ability to delete an expense.\n\n\nPantry stock updates and low-stock alerts are confirmed, along with the correct suggested shopping list. Market purchases are simulated, confirming quantity updates, transaction logging, and spending updates.\n\nBudget recalculation tests show accurate remaining budget calculation and correct alert triggers for both budget running low and exceeded scenarios.\n\nFinally, reminder notifications, including overdue and upcoming bills, are verified through an API call.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"@'\\nconst http = require('http');\\n\\nfunction request(options, data) {\\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n    co